CEUME-v1.0 Production Publishing Specification & Build Pipeline
Project Designation: Cosmos-Encrypted Universe Mapping Engine (CEUME) Monograph
Publisher Style Standard: Academic Monograph (Springer / SIAM / Cambridge Standards)
Lead System Designer: C. Matthew Blackwell
1. Publisher-Grade Typography & Style Preamble (book_preamble.sty)
To elevate the manuscript to a professional 500-page monograph standard, integrate the following complete typographic, mathematical, and hyper-metadata configurations into your centralized style file.
\ProvidesPackage{book_preamble}

\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}
\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}
\usepackage{amsmath, amssymb, amsthm, mathtools}
\usepackage{geometry}
\usepackage{booktabs}
\usepackage{microtype}
\usepackage{graphicx}
\usepackage{listings}
\usepackage{xcolor}
\usepackage{siunitx}
\usepackage{caption}
\usepackage{makeidx}
\usepackage[acronym]{glossaries}

% Publisher Font Stack
\usepackage{libertinus}
\usepackage{inconsolata}

% Geometry configuration for binding offset and professional margins
\geometry{
    paper=a4paper,
    inner=30mm,
    outer=25mm,
    top=25mm,
    bottom=25mm,
    bindingoffset=10mm
}

% Chapter Style & Layout Enforcement
\chapterstyle{hangnum}
\setsecnumformat{\csname the#1\endcsname\quad}
\aliaspagestyle{chapter}{empty}
\openright

% Caption Formatting
\captionsetup{labelfont=bf, font=small}

% Mathematical Environments via thmtools
\usepackage{thmtools}
\declaretheoremstyle[
    spaceabove=12pt,
    spacebelow=12pt,
    headfont=\bfseries,
    bodyfont=\normalfont,
]{ceume-style}
\declaretheorem[style=ceume-style, numberwithin=chapter]{theorem}
\declaretheorem[style=ceume-style, numbered=no]{definition}
\declaretheorem[style=ceume-style, numbered=no]{lemma}

% TikZ Externalization for High-Performance Build Times
\usepackage{tikz}
\usetikzlibrary{external}
\tikzexternalize[prefix=figures/tikz/]

% Publisher-Grade BibLaTeX Configuration
\usepackage[
    backend=biber,
    style=alphabetic,
    sorting=nyt,
    maxbibnames=10
]{biblatex}

% Index and Glossary Generation
\makeindex
\makeglossaries

% Hyperref Metadata Embedding
\usepackage{hyperref}
\hypersetup{
    colorlinks=true,
    linkcolor=blue!50!black,
    citecolor=green!50!black,
    urlcolor=red!50!black,
    pdftitle={Cosmos-Encrypted Universe Mapping Engine},
    pdfauthor={C. Matthew Blackwell},
    pdfsubject={Encrypted Cosmological Simulation Framework},
    pdfkeywords={FHE, CKKS, HEALPix, MPI, Cosmology, Simulation}
}

2. Frontmatter, Index, and Glossary Architecture
To satisfy publisher requirements for a 500-page monograph, auxiliary files must be initialized and structured as follows:
A. Acronym Definition (acronyms.tex)
\newacronym{ceume}{CEUME}{Cosmos-Encrypted Universe Mapping Engine}
\newacronym{fhe}{FHE}{Fully Homomorphic Encryption}
\newacronym{ckks}{CKKS}{Cheon-Kim-Kim-Song Homomorphic Encryption Scheme}
\newacronym{healpix}{HEALPix}{Hierarchical Equal Area isoLatitude Pixelisation}
\newacronym{mpi}{MPI}{Message Passing Interface}
\newacronym{mhd}{MHD}{Magnetohydrodynamics}

B. Glossary Definition (glossary.tex)
\newglossaryentry{multiplicative_depth}{
    name=multiplicative depth,
    description={The count of sequential homomorphic multiplications executed on a ciphertext before noise accumulation requires key refreshing or bootstrapping.}
}
\newglossaryentry{healpix}{
    name=HEALPix,
    description={A mathematical framework and pixelization standard that partitions the sphere into equal-area quadrangular cells.}
}

3. Automated Monograph Build Pipeline (latexmkrc or Build Script)
Compiling a complex 500-page manuscript with externalized graphics, indexes, acronyms, and bibliographic databases requires an automated, multi-pass build workflow.
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# ==============================================================================
# CEUME-v1.0 Monograph Automated Build Script
# Architect: C. Matthew Blackwell (Independent Designer)
# ==============================================================================

echo "[CEUME BUILD] Initializing master document compilation..."

# Step 1: Initial PDF compilation & auxiliary generation via latexmk
latexmk -pdf -pdflatex="pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -synctex=1" main.tex

# Step 2: Process bibliography database via Biber
echo "[CEUME BUILD] Processing bibliography database..."
biber main

# Step 3: Compile index and glossaries
echo "[CEUME BUILD] Generating index and glossary tables..."
makeindex main.idx
makeglossaries main

# Step 4: Final stabilization passes
echo "[CEUME BUILD] Executing final multi-pass stabilization..."
latexmk -pdf -pdflatex="pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode" main.tex

echo "[CEUME BUILD] Build complete. Monograph compiled successfully."

